the charred wreckage of the bus makes  clear how intense the fire must have  been  the vehicle crashed and burned on a  bulgarian highway in the middle of the  night it was taking mostly north  macedonian tourists back home after a  weekend trip to istanbul but it's not  yet known why so few people made it off  alive or what caused this disaster in  the first place this damage suggests the  bus hit a barrier before carrying on to  crash into the central reservation  bulgaria's interior minister said he was  deeply shocked by what he'd seen  not everyone can stand such a picture  the picture is terrifying  the details of this tragedy will be  investigated  north macedonia's foreign minister  visited survivors in hospital in  bulgaria's capital sophia  i'm here in the hospital to get more  information what we know is that a  horrible tragedy has happened here in  bulgaria with the bus that carried north  macedonia nationals who were traveling  from istanbul to scorpio there were over  53 passengers on the bus dozens of them  are children over 40 were killed some of  the wounded were transferred here but  let me first see the situation and i'll  be back later with more  police in north macedonia have begun an  investigation into bezatrans the bus and  travel company  this man came to its shuttered office in  north macedonia's capital skopje looking  for news of his nephew  i saw information about the crash at 6am  this morning i saw it on the internet  and as my nephew was in turkey i started  searching on the internet  i called bezetrans for the number for  three four hours we do not have any  information for them nor are they  answering their phone  and the investigation continues by  daylight on the struma highway into the  worst bus crash in bulgarian history  rory challenge now to zero
 

